      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( b \\), we first need to solve the equation \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\) for \\( x \\).\n\n1. **Solve the equation \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\)**:\n\n   Subtract 7 from both sides: \\[\n   2x + 7 - 7 = 3 - 7 \\Rightarrow 2x = -4\n   \\]\n\nNext, divide both sides by 2: \\[\n2x = -4 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{-4}{2} \\Rightarrow x = -2\n   \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( x = -2 \\), we substitute this value into the second equation \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\) and solve for \\( b \\):\n\n2. **Substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the equation \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\)**:\n\n   \\[\n   b(-2) - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n\n   Simplify the equation: \\[\n   -2b - 10 = -2\n   \\]\n\n   Add 10 to both sides: \\[\n   -2b - 10 + 10 = -2 + 10 \\Rightarrow -2b = 8\n   \\]\n\nNow, divide both sides by -2 to find \\( b \\): \\[\n-2b = 8 \\Rightarrow b = \\frac{8}{-2} \\Rightarrow b = -4\n   \\]\n\n  Therefore, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
